say whether a coordinated read ran, and for what

An application that cannot read a file it can plainly list shows empty content and reports nothing.
That is what #190 and #192 both looked like from outside, and neither could be told apart from the
application simply choosing not to read.

Three lines on CIDER_TRACE_FILECOORD: the ask with its URL and options, then either run with the
resolved URL or REFUSED with the error. A refusal and a read that never happened want opposite fixes.

Measured on iA Writer, where the library rows say Updating and the editor pane is blank, and it
disproved the obvious explanation in one run: every read RAN, including the clicked document.

  CIDER_FILECOORD read ask Documents options=0x0
  CIDER_FILECOORD read run Documents
  CIDER_FILECOORD read ask Documents/Cider.md options=0x1
  CIDER_FILECOORD read run Documents/Cider.md

So the file contents reach the application and the empty editor is downstream of that.

--- a/src/NSFileCoordinator.m
+++ b/src/NSFileCoordinator.m
@@ -703,15 +703,36 @@
 
 - (void)coordinateReadingItemAtURL: (NSURL*)url options:(NSFileCoordinatorReadingOptions)options error: (NSError**)outError byAccessor: (void (^)(NSURL* newURL))reader
 {
+	/* WHETHER THE ACCESSOR RAN, and for which file. An application that cannot read a file it can
+	 * plainly list shows empty content and no error of its own, which is what #190 and #192 both
+	 * looked like from outside. A refusal here and a read that simply never happened want opposite
+	 * fixes, so both are printed. */
+	BOOL trace = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_FILECOORD") != NULL && getenv("CIDER_TRACE_FILECOORD")[0] != '\0';
+	if (trace) {
+		fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_FILECOORD read ask %s options=0x%lx\n",
+		        [[url path] UTF8String] ?: "(nil)", (unsigned long) options);
+		fflush(stderr);
+	}
 	// no need to copy `reader` block because we are synchronous
 	NSFileAccessIntent* intent = [NSFileAccessIntent readingIntentWithURL: url options: options];
 	[self submitIntent: intent onQueue: nil withBlock: ^(NSError* error) {
 		if (error) {
+			if (trace) {
+				fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_FILECOORD read REFUSED %s error=%s\n",
+				        [[url path] UTF8String] ?: "(nil)",
+				        [[error description] UTF8String] ?: "(nil)");
+				fflush(stderr);
+			}
 			if (outError) {
 				*outError = error;
 			}
 			return;
 		} else {
+			if (trace) {
+				fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_FILECOORD read run %s\n",
+				        [[intent.URL path] UTF8String] ?: "(nil)");
+				fflush(stderr);
+			}
 			reader(intent.URL);
 		}
 	}];
